Public signatures can leak private names even if the table is
correct. If \texttt{Charts.Grid} has a public constructor that
returns an internal-only error type, either export an appropriate
public route for the error, hide its identity behind an abstraction,
or reject the signature under the language's accessibility rules.
Do not silently insert the error into the public table: that would
turn an incidental implementation choice into a compatibility
commitment.

